James Rising received an email from Oyshi Islam, a graduate student with a strong academic background in Fisheries Science and current research in various fish biology topics. Oyshi expressed admiration for James's work on climate impacts, seeking an opportunity to conduct graduate studies under his supervision. James's response thanked Oyshi for her interest and outlined the impressive nature of her work but conveyed that he is unable to accept new students this year due to commitments and funding constraints. He offered to discuss potential collaborations in the future and provided a link for scheduling a brief Zoom meeting.
